    slice0: the compiler's gates become required jobs of the CI workflow (scripts/checks/compiler/), and the trust ban admits the compiler library and its pinned dependency
    
    Train 32743e40 failed main's CI run 42450324302 twice over:
    - Root checks ran the slice-0 gates (run.sh runs every scripts/checks/*.sh) in the gates shell,
      which has no Lean by design: `lake: not found`, and build_identity.sh refused outside the devshell.
    - Proof trust ban refused lakefile.toml: `require` and the Concrete library were not allow-listed.
    
    The gates move to scripts/checks/compiler/ (README: gates stay in scripts/checks, no scripts/compiler/),
    so they are no longer root checks; slice0.yml's jobs join lean_action_ci.yml, each gated on the
    landing record, and every matrix leg is named in required-checks.txt. landing_script.sh now names a
    matrix job's legs as GitHub shows them (include rows only; anything else is refused), with controls.
    trust_ban.sh allows exactly the libraries ConcreteSpec and Concrete and a `require` pinned to a full
    commit that lake-manifest.json records at the same URL and commit, with five controls; the two old
    lakefile controls now assert their reason instead of any refusal. README gate 2 states that the
    compiler's trust gate is not yet a job.
